<h1>HerbHaul drivers — founding roster</h1>
<p><a href="/admin">← Dashboard</a></p>
<p class="muted">
  Counts and cities only — <strong>no driver names or emails ever appear here or in any
  dispensary-facing export.</strong> This page aggregates the founding driver list
  (waitlist signups with the drive role) so coverage by market can be planned without
  exposing anyone's identity.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  <strong>With-app count note:</strong> founding-driver Gmails added to the HerbHaul Driver
  tester list are tracked in the house ledger in the goal workspace, not in this database —
  so this page currently passes an empty app-holder set and the with-app count reads
  <strong>0</strong> even after tester invites go out. It becomes real when the ledger is wired in.
</p>

<h2>Founding drivers</h2>
<% if (!roster.total) { %>
  <p class="muted">No founding drivers yet — nobody has joined the drive list.</p>
<% } else { %>
  <p>Total founding drivers: <strong><%= roster.total %></strong><br>
  Already holding the driver app: <strong><%= roster.withApp %></strong></p>

  <h3>By state</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Drivers</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    <% roster.byState.forEach(function(s) { %>
      <tr><td><%= s.state %></td><td><strong><%= s.count %></strong></td></tr>
    <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>By city</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>City</th><th>State</th><th>Drivers</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    <% roster.byCity.forEach(function(c) { %>
      <tr><td><%= c.city %></td><td><%= c.state %></td><td><strong><%= c.count %></strong></td></tr>
    <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="muted">Machine-readable counts: <a href="/admin/cannadash-drivers.json">/admin/cannadash-drivers.json</a> (same counts, no identities).</p>
<% } %>
